    "source_file_to_entries": {
        "raw-wiktextract-data.jsonl": [
            {
                "entry_id": "f9203f96-64e2-3274-997c-7bb9d296fec4",
                "word": "interanimate",
                "pos": "adj",
                "lang_code": "en",
                "forms": [],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "3b4cc293-3cd1-3a69-afa5-32aa470bd71d",
                        "entry_id": "f9203f96-64e2-3274-997c-7bb9d296fec4",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Occurring as or involving interactions between separate consciousnesses."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "not-comparable"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "ee8aff9d-33d4-4e07-a39a-0a0f05a64065",
                                "sense_id": "3b4cc293-3cd1-3a69-afa5-32aa470bd71d",
                                "text": "Meanwhile, however, classicism had kept alive the imagination of an interanimate cosmos: of the land and the sea as gods and as comprising hosts of minor local deities; of humans as children of gods; of natural creatures as transformed humans (Daphne into laurel, Procne into swallow) or as transformable into human shape."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "25fcefb0-de05-4f24-a659-ca74800dc95b",
                                "sense_id": "3b4cc293-3cd1-3a69-afa5-32aa470bd71d",
                                "text": "Before going on to show the relationship of tactile-kinesthetic invariants and iconicity to analogical thinking, I would like to interpose a question alluded to earlier: how are new interanimate meanings minted?"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "4a4d014b-90bf-4fdd-a939-5ece37e4c758",
                                "sense_id": "3b4cc293-3cd1-3a69-afa5-32aa470bd71d",
                                "text": "Deepened understandings of responsivity, of its basis in both comsigns and interchangeability, and of the basis of comsigns and interchangeability in species-specific kinetic/tactile-kinesthetic invariants, provide the grounds for elucidating the interanimate phenomenon of empathy."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "dc69ac81-1692-4d5f-837e-40d82de96bae",
                                "sense_id": "3b4cc293-3cd1-3a69-afa5-32aa470bd71d",
                                "text": "The beauty of the queer invitation, Forster discovers, lies in its unconventional temporality, which permits delays, demurrals, and even extended deferrals, but which nonetheless supplies a lifeline for interanimate collaborations that interrupt the self's consolidation into an obedient disciple of heterosexuality."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "bbf00396-927e-3cf2-9eaa-7767a5e0e616",
                        "entry_id": "f9203f96-64e2-3274-997c-7bb9d296fec4",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Mutually affecting; tending to interanimate."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "not-comparable"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "74738421-6b3c-44c9-97c9-38496e16b46f",
                                "sense_id": "bbf00396-927e-3cf2-9eaa-7767a5e0e616",
                                "text": "If we agree with Pat Hartwell's statement that thinking and writing are interanimate, then we cannot help but address thinking when we speak of writing ."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "c26d0657-a0eb-4145-85c6-28771bce2971",
                                "sense_id": "bbf00396-927e-3cf2-9eaa-7767a5e0e616",
                                "text": "The interaction of discourses is dynamic, interdependent, \"interanimate,\" and \"interilluminating.\""
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "1c4be858-c44e-407d-ba54-f6035095e6ca",
                                "sense_id": "bbf00396-927e-3cf2-9eaa-7767a5e0e616",
                                "text": "In chapter five, the applied chapter, I show how ecological and prima facie formalist and aesthetic values are interanimate and therefore inseparable."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [],
                "word_linkages": []
            },
