                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "8e27b58a-2c9c-3cd5-9381-281b324ffd2c",
                        "entry_id": "b5908120-b304-3055-8bbe-5b8d5550ab2b",
                        "glosses": [
                            "To animate or inspire mutually."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "f9238a63-1c46-4bff-8f9a-d6bdf818a267",
                                "sense_id": "8e27b58a-2c9c-3cd5-9381-281b324ffd2c",
                                "text": "When love, with another so\nInteranimates two souls"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "3910e066-699c-43e9-886e-cbecbfa6d2b6",
                                "sense_id": "8e27b58a-2c9c-3cd5-9381-281b324ffd2c",
                                "text": "These voices compete, interanimate (penetrate and inform), and change over time."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "14bed87c-9455-4e86-a75b-2c8d6098bf25",
                                "sense_id": "8e27b58a-2c9c-3cd5-9381-281b324ffd2c",
                                "text": "The third space enables new meanings to be generated as the diverse voices of the official script and unofficial counterscript interanimate."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "6a537ca0-ba4c-49cf-82e1-f2beac0716a8",
                                "sense_id": "8e27b58a-2c9c-3cd5-9381-281b324ffd2c",
                                "text": "As cognitive, aesthetic, and ethical discourses accumulate, and juxtapose, Bakhtin (1990) argues they begin to interanimate, to show up in one another, to express one through the other."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
